# Build outputs
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.local

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
# package-lock.json was ignored here, and the Dockerfile ran `npm install`,
# so every image build re-resolved the ranges in package.json against whatever
# npm considered newest at that moment. On 2026-09-20 that produced
# react 19.2.5 against react-dom 19.2.4 -- a mismatched pair React refuses to
# run (error #527), so the built app was a blank page. `npm run build` passed
# throughout, because a bundler does not check that the two agree at runtime.
# The lock is tracked now and the Dockerfile uses `npm ci`.

